WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.834
-Lili, I wanted
to ask you about a tweet

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:04.400
that you tweeted out
that made me laugh.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.267
Because you were at Coachella
and you tweeted out,

00:00:06.267 --> 00:00:09.667
"Where can I get a Mountain Dew
at Coachella?"

00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:10.901
[ Laughter ]

00:00:10.901 --> 00:00:13.734
Was it hard to get a --
-Couldn't find one.

00:00:13.734 --> 00:00:16.300
Never found one.
And that was at 10:20 p.m.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.968
So you know I wasn't entirely...

00:00:18.968 --> 00:00:20.901
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.901 --> 00:00:23.934
-Dehydrated. Okay. That's it.
Sorry, sorry.

00:00:23.934 --> 00:00:25.734
I hate to put words
in your mouth. Yeah.

00:00:25.734 --> 00:00:27.834
But you do the Dew.
You're a Mountain Dew --

00:00:27.834 --> 00:00:31.601
-I do the Dew. My mom drank it
when I was in the womb.

00:00:31.601 --> 00:00:33.033
It's her fault.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.534
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:36.133
-No way. Come on.
-Yes. Yes.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:38.501
-I thought it would be kind of
fun if you and I maybe --

00:00:38.501 --> 00:00:41.234
There's a few different
Mountain Dew-inspired products.

00:00:41.234 --> 00:00:42.901
These are real.
-Mm-hmm. Right, right.

00:00:42.901 --> 00:00:45.501
-Not paid for by Mountain Dew,
but I thought we could give it

00:00:45.501 --> 00:00:47.501
a try and see what you think.
-Yeah, let's try

00:00:47.501 --> 00:00:49.300
some Mountain Dew products.
-This is for you.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:50.734
This is a lip balm.
-Ooh!

00:00:50.734 --> 00:00:52.634
-This is a Mountain Dew
lip balm.

00:00:52.634 --> 00:00:54.033
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.033 --> 00:00:56.667
-Ooh, it's darker
than you would expect.

00:00:56.667 --> 00:00:59.000
-It is. Mountain Dew
is not this dark a green.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.067
-A little bit of a scent.
Like a lime.

00:01:01.067 --> 00:01:02.801
-Yeah. A little bit of a lime.
Okay.

00:01:02.801 --> 00:01:04.367
-I don't want to mess up my --

00:01:04.367 --> 00:01:05.968
-Oh, yeah. Your lipstick.
Yeah, me neither.

00:01:05.968 --> 00:01:07.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:09.100
Let me see. Hey.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:11.501
-Moisturizing.
-Not bad.

00:01:11.501 --> 00:01:13.501
-Yeah, that was okay.

00:01:13.501 --> 00:01:14.767
-Yeah.

00:01:14.767 --> 00:01:16.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.267 --> 00:01:18.834
Yeah. I like this. Not bad.

00:01:18.834 --> 00:01:20.834
I give this a --
-It's like a six out of ten.

00:01:20.834 --> 00:01:22.701
-Six out of ten. Sure.
I'll give it a seven.

00:01:22.701 --> 00:01:24.300
-Okay.
-Alright. That's good.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:26.367
Oh. Ready for this one?
-Yeah. Yeah. Ooh.

00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:27.901
This is scary.
-This one's very interesting.

00:01:27.901 --> 00:01:31.434
It's Mountain Dew-inspired
ice cream called Mountain Moo.

00:01:31.434 --> 00:01:34.167
It's made by Moo-Ville Creamery
in Michigan.

00:01:34.167 --> 00:01:36.100
We got it sent to us
just for you.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:37.834
Mountain Moo.
-Aww. How kind.

00:01:37.834 --> 00:01:40.634
-Here we go.
Oh, you need a spoon. Sorry.

00:01:40.634 --> 00:01:42.767
You're like, "How do I eat it?"
Yeah. Okay. Here we go.

00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:44.367
Alright. It's the right color.

00:01:44.367 --> 00:01:48.000
♪♪

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.234 --> 00:01:53.234
-I would not go out of my way
to eat this.

00:01:53.234 --> 00:01:54.834
-It's kind of interesting.
I don't know wh--

00:01:54.834 --> 00:01:56.634
It doesn't quite make
the right turn, does it?

00:01:56.634 --> 00:02:00.734
-It tastes like the flavor of
milk after you have Froot Loops.

00:02:00.734 --> 00:02:03.267
Like, the milk afterwards.
-Now I'm jumping back in.

00:02:03.267 --> 00:02:05.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:08.567
-[ Laughs ] Take another.

00:02:08.567 --> 00:02:10.300
Don't you kind of think?

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:12.267
-I kind of like that.
Now I like it more.

00:02:12.267 --> 00:02:15.067
-If you think of it going in --
-Tastes like Froot Loops milk.

00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:17.133
-Yeah.
I would not eat that again, no.

00:02:17.133 --> 00:02:18.701
-I would. I would totally do it.

00:02:18.701 --> 00:02:20.234
You totally sold me on it now
and changed it.

00:02:20.234 --> 00:02:21.467
-Okay. [ Laughs ]
-Yeah.

00:02:21.467 --> 00:02:23.601
This next one is
an alcohol-related product.

00:02:23.601 --> 00:02:25.734
-Okay. I'm old enough.

00:02:25.734 --> 00:02:27.400
-Here we go. Let's pretend
we're at Coachella.

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:28.534
-Oh!
-Here you go.

00:02:28.534 --> 00:02:30.634
-This would be a dream
at Coachella.

00:02:30.634 --> 00:02:33.234
-This is a distillery. It's
a Mountain Dew-inspired vodka

00:02:33.234 --> 00:02:37.000
called --
by Three Olives in Jersey City.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:38.467
-Okay.
-Okay.

00:02:38.467 --> 00:02:40.834
-This flavor is called --
ready for this -- Dude.

00:02:40.834 --> 00:02:42.501
-Dude.
-Yeah. Cheers.

00:02:42.501 --> 00:02:44.701
-Cheers.
-Cheers, dude.

00:02:44.701 --> 00:02:49.000
♪♪

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.467
[ Mouths word ]

00:02:51.467 --> 00:02:54.534
-It is actually not as bad
as I thought it was going to be.

00:02:54.534 --> 00:02:58.701
-That's not bad. But this one --
I would do Dude.

00:02:58.701 --> 00:03:00.634
[ Laughter ]
-Mmm.

00:03:00.634 --> 00:03:03.100
But this one -- The next one,
this last one here,

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:04.834
this is a real --
I have not tried this.

00:03:04.834 --> 00:03:07.200
I thought maybe we could
try this together. This is real.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.734
This is Mountain Dew
Flamin' Hot.

00:03:09.734 --> 00:03:12.133
[ Woman in audience cheers ]

00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:13.901
Have you ever tried this?

00:03:13.901 --> 00:03:17.167
-I'm such an original Dew girl
that I don't...

00:03:17.167 --> 00:03:18.701
-The orange?

00:03:18.701 --> 00:03:20.634
-...partake in Code Red
or anything like that.

00:03:20.634 --> 00:03:22.801
So this is scary.

00:03:22.801 --> 00:03:24.734
-Smells good.

00:03:24.734 --> 00:03:27.100
♪♪

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:29.400
Ooh. It's g-- No.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:30.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.701 --> 00:03:31.801
-Ooh. It is spicy!

00:03:31.801 --> 00:03:33.601
-It's got a burn after-taste
to it.

00:03:33.601 --> 00:03:36.534
-Yeah, it's a little bit
of burn in me.

00:03:36.534 --> 00:03:38.467
-Sorry. You want more Dude?

00:03:38.467 --> 00:03:41.601
-No, I'm okay. Well, maybe.
Let's take a little bit more.

00:03:41.601 --> 00:03:42.734
-Take a Dude.
-Wash it down?

00:03:42.734 --> 00:03:44.400
-Wash it down. There you go.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:46.200
Thank you for trying
that stuff with me, pal.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:47.868
-Ooh. That's not good.

00:03:47.868 --> 00:03:49.400
-Now, look. Here we go.

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:50.901
-It's worse the second time.

00:03:50.901 --> 00:03:53.634
-I want to talk
about your movie.

00:03:53.634 --> 00:03:55.400
-Okay.
-"Look Both Ways."

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:57.400
-Yes. "Look Both Ways."
-Congratulations.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.334
You produced this, as well.
-Thank you. I did. Yeah.

00:03:59.334 --> 00:04:01.133
-Do you like producing?
-I do.

00:04:01.133 --> 00:04:03.300
I love to be
in control of things.

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:05.100
-You do?
-I really do.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:07.467
-You get a little --
You get some voice.

00:04:07.467 --> 00:04:09.801
You get to go...
-Well, yeah, because, you know,

00:04:09.801 --> 00:04:12.634
it's better to have
the "executive producer" title,

00:04:12.634 --> 00:04:15.467
otherwise you're just,
like, a bossy actor.

00:04:15.467 --> 00:04:17.234
-Yeah.
-Rather than I'm like,

00:04:17.234 --> 00:04:18.834
"No, no, I have this title.

00:04:18.834 --> 00:04:20.501
I'm allowed
to make these decisions."

00:04:20.501 --> 00:04:21.901
-Yeah, you are. Yeah.

00:04:21.901 --> 00:04:23.300
-So it makes me feel good, yes.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.667
-How do we describe
"Look Both Ways"?

00:04:25.667 --> 00:04:26.968
I like the idea of this.

00:04:26.968 --> 00:04:29.534
-"Look Both Ways."
It follows Natalie

00:04:29.534 --> 00:04:33.200
on the eve of her graduation --
college graduation.

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:34.734
She takes a pregnancy test,

00:04:34.734 --> 00:04:39.400
and her life severs off into
two different parallel lives,

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:42.801
one where she is pregnant
and one where she's not.

00:04:42.801 --> 00:04:44.767
And I think what I loved most
about the movie

00:04:44.767 --> 00:04:48.067
and when I read the script
was that there is no wrong path.

00:04:48.067 --> 00:04:51.334
There isn't one that you're like
"Oh, that was the bad one."

00:04:51.334 --> 00:04:55.033
So I think both --
There's silver linings in both.

00:04:55.033 --> 00:04:59.367
And it's comforting to know
that there isn't one decision

00:04:59.367 --> 00:05:01.934
that you can make
that will just completely derail

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:03.801
everything in your world.

00:05:03.801 --> 00:05:04.968
-Well said.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:04.968 --> 00:05:07.534
Here's Lili Reinhart
in "Look Both Ways."

00:05:07.534 --> 00:05:08.734
Take a look.

00:05:08.734 --> 00:05:10.234
-They're probably
just not expecting it

00:05:10.234 --> 00:05:11.601
to play out that way.

00:05:11.601 --> 00:05:15.000
-They weren't ex--
I wasn't expecting this.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:18.300
I did not see

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:22.534
"single unemployed
22-year-old mom"

00:05:22.534 --> 00:05:25.734
on my tarot card reading
that Kara gave me last month.

00:05:25.734 --> 00:05:28.601
-What about our plans?

00:05:28.601 --> 00:05:32.567
What about naked Sundays
and furniture with sharp edges?

00:05:32.567 --> 00:05:34.467
We were supposed to go
to Barcelona next year!

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:37.834
-I've been thinking
about that quite a bit.

00:05:37.834 --> 00:05:40.400
It would make sense if...

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:41.634
-What?

00:05:41.634 --> 00:05:44.934
-If you and I just --

00:05:44.934 --> 00:05:47.300
[ Indistinct arguing outside ]

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:48.734
If, um...

00:05:48.734 --> 00:05:50.234
-It's not gonna be --
Oh, no. Unh-unh!

00:05:50.234 --> 00:05:51.434
-Let's get married.

00:05:51.434 --> 00:05:53.534
-No! Nuh-unh! No! Get up!
That's not happening!

00:05:53.534 --> 00:05:55.000
-Hey! Hey!
-Get up!

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:57.133
-Yeah! Lili Reinhart, everybody!

00:05:57.133 --> 00:05:59.234
"Look Both Ways"
begins streaming

00:05:59.234 --> 00:06:01.501
August 17th on Netflix.

00:06:01.501 --> 00:06:03.067
We'll be right back
with more "Tonight Show."

00:06:03.067 --> 00:06:04.634
Stick around, everybody.

